        "abstract": "DEM is a powerful technique that relies on a rather counterintuitive idea: DAC elements can be shuffled to turn nonlinearities caused by unknown mismatches into noise, thus making a DAC linear on average. In this tutorial article we discuss DEM in the context of unary-weighted DACs in a way that requires little to no background. We tackle the topic in a non-architecture-specific fashion, and mostly focus on how the technique works.",
