        "abstract": "The article highlights the role of open-source initiatives in technological innovation through the IEEE CAS Society’s grand challenges. The challenges act as catalysts, bridging academic research, industry needs, and creativity to produce open-source datasets, ML/DL models, and setting performance benchmarks. The development of open-source datasets involves complex data collection and maintenance processes, balancing data quality with privacy concerns. The grand challenges are structured in stages, with strict rules to maintain integrity and foster innovation. These initiatives contribute significantly to the development of industry standards, with participants influencing standardization processes. The case study on the Respiratory Sound Grand Challenge exemplifies this impact, demonstrating the challenges’ role in advancing digital stethoscope technology and setting up the stage for IEEE Digital Stethoscope Standard Working Group, P3435 with industry benchmarks.",
